From 86e44bcd065e81174b7cfe0adb4b2366eb3f3e2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Jones <grahamjonesgs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:33:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] KlaussCPU: built-in klausscpu-unknown-linux-musl target,
 so rustc can run on it

- Arch::KlaussCpu (was Arch::Other("klausscpu") from the JSON specs; the
  JSON "klausscpu" string now parses to it), threaded through callconv,
  va_arg, target features, inline asm (unsupported), c-variadic status,
  scalable vectors, miri's malloc alignment.
- targets/klausscpu_unknown_linux_musl.rs: the Linux JSON spec built in
  (tier 3, host tools): PIC by default (needed for dylibs and the host
  tools), thread-locals on, relro, uwtable, static CRT by default; clang
  links, with the musl sysroot's crt objects and libunwind.
- rustc_codegen_ssa: the object crate cannot write KlaussCPU ELF, so the
  objects rustc writes itself (metadata wrappers, a dylib's .rustc
  metadata, the linked-symbols object) are ELF32-LE i386 objects given
  KlaussCPU's e_machine and e_flags.  They never hold code or relocations.
  Without them a dylib's metadata went to the linker raw (read as a linker
  script) and a dylib lost its exported code.
- bootstrap: no self-contained musl objects for klausscpu (it links the
  sysroot's), and klausscpu-unknown-linux-musl in STAGE0_MISSING_TARGETS.

